ctive evidence every day that you  are gay you know if you're a man the  plumbing tells you there's nothing else  right and you twist and deform your  whole psyche and tell yourself crazy  stories and you tell yourself that black  is white  in the top is bottom and Northeast South  in order to deny this obvious fact and  that's what I was you can talk about  your kind of you were living life as a  photographic negative yeah  it's everything is in proportion  everything else everything seems logical  and yet it's all completely backwards  and that's pretty much where your  soullessness came from right because you  were so inverted that you you couldn't  really afford an interior life yeah I  couldn't have an interior life I felt  that I was a monster incapable of love  you know love to me would have to mean  love for a man and that to me could not  be love that was some kind of strange  wacko psychosis I had so you know the  ability to love is the very center of  the soul for most people you know it  kind of defines our personality and  without that you're kind of you know I I  was hollowed out I was doing everything  else in life I was looking and acting  mostly normal but I went around with  this certain interior knowledge that I  alone among all of human beings had been  born without the capacity to love you  know one of the things that I think is  so memorable and touching about the book  and interesting is that it is you say  you're you you are not claiming that you  were a typical teenager that you were a  typical gay person whatever but there's  clearly an exemplary nature that reaches  beyond issues of sexuality to you know  yeah and Nick the biggest surprise to me  of this book ever since I first started  showing it to people you know I wrote it  for myself thinking I was describing  this kind of crazy pathology and wanted  to get it on paper before I lost touch  with it  it was receding disappearing like a  dream and when I showed it to people  especially s